==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|outside|er}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌaʊtˈsaɪdəɹ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is not part of a [[community]] or [[organization]].
#: {{ux|en|While the initiated easily understand the symbols, they are wholly inaccessible to '''outsiders'''.}}
# A [[newcomer]] with little or no experience in an organization or community.
#: {{ux|en|Seeing the mess professional politicians have made of things is it any wonder the electorate is beginning to prefer '''outsiders'''.}}
# A [[competitor]] or [[contestant]] who has little [[chance]] of [[winning]]; a [[long shot]]
#: {{ux|en|Johnny was an '''outsider''' at this years karate tournament, but he still managed to win second place out of sheer determination.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|someone excluded}} {{l|en|stranger}}; see also [[Thesaurus:outcast]] or [[Thesaurus:foreigner]]
* {{sense|a newcomer}} {{l|en|newling}}; see also [[Thesaurus:newcomer]]
* {{sense|a long shot}} {{l|en|dark horse}}, {{l|en|little guy}}, {{l|en|underdog}}

